{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1357-online-learning-in-betting-markets-profit.md", "equation": "Verdict:** ADAPT — the binary-market model with Kelly bettors yields two directly reusable results for GSE: (1) the closed-form fair-odds price a⋆ = √(g·E[p_t])/(√(g·E[p_t]) + √((1−g)(1−E[p_t]))) plus an FTL algorithm with O(√(T log T)) high-probability regret, which models how prediction-market prices converge and gives GSE a benchmark for its own probability estimates; (2) the \"heavier tails in bettor beliefs → higher bookmaker profit\" theorem, which tells GSE exactly when books will shade lines against informed flow — but the paper's bookmaker-side framing must be inverted since GSE is the bettor/information platform, not the house.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1357-online-learning-in-betting-markets-profit.md", "equation": "Algorithm 2 (fair odds, Sec. 5):** Follow-the-Leader-type (after Frongillo et al. 2012); fair-odds profit u(a, 1−a) is concave in a with closed-form maximizer a⋆ = √(g·E[p_t]) / (√(g·E[p_t]) + √((1−g)(1−E[p_t]))) (eq. 27); empirical mean p̄_T plugged in, with clipping to (τ, 1−τ).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1357-online-learning-in-betting-markets-profit.md", "equation": "SA update: a_{t+1} = a_t + η_t(p̄_t − a_t − G(a_t)) (Alg. 1); h(a) = a + G(a) − E[p_t | p_t ≥ a].", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1357-online-learning-in-betting-markets-profit.md", "equation": "Thm. 5.1 (fair):** u_t(a_T,b_T) ≥ u_t(a⋆,b⋆) − L·T^{−1/2}·√log(1/δ) with probability ≥ 1−δ; **Cor. 5.2:** REGRET(T, a⋆, b⋆) = O(√(T log T)).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
