{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1367-kelly-criterion-simple-random-walk-levy-processes.md", "equation": "Long-term growth rate gr(f) = lim_{n→∞} (1/n)·ln(W_n^f/W_0) = E[ln(1 + f·r)] (eq. 2.5), justified by the strong law of large numbers (Prop 2.1).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1367-kelly-criterion-simple-random-walk-levy-processes.md", "equation": "General growth rate:** gr(f) = E[ln(1 + f·r)] (eq. 2.5); wealth asymptotics W_n^f = exp(n·gr(f)·(1 + ε_n)), ε_n → 0 a.s. (Prop 2.1, eqs. 2.6–2.8).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1367-kelly-criterion-simple-random-walk-levy-processes.md", "equation": "CLT refinement:** W_n^f = exp(n·gr(f) + √n·σ_r(f)·ζ_n + ϵ_n) with σ_r(f) = (E[ln²(1+fr)] − gr²(f))^{1/2}, ζ_n standard Gaussian (Thm 2.1, eq. 2.10) — finite-horizon wealth confidence bands.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1367-kelly-criterion-simple-random-walk-levy-processes.md", "equation": "Concavity:** dgr/df = E[r/(1+fr)], d²gr/df² = −E[r²/(1+fr)²] < 0 (Prop 2.2, eq. 2.11); gr continuous on [0,1], unique maximizer f* ∈ [0,1] with gr(f*) ≥ 0 (Cor 2.1).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1367-kelly-criterion-simple-random-walk-levy-processes.md", "equation": "High-frequency limit:** n bets per unit time with r_{n,k} = μ/n + (σ/√n)·ξ_{n,k} ⇒ wealth converges in law to W_t^f = exp((fμ − f²σ²/2)·t + fσ·B_t) (Thm 4.1, eq. 4.5).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1367-kelly-criterion-simple-random-walk-levy-processes.md", "equation": "Lognormal closed form:** for P_{t} = e^{bt+σB_t}, optimal f* = b/σ² + 1/2 (Thm 4.2, eq. 4.16); numerical check with σ = 1, n = 10: optimal f_{10}* \"very close\" to eq. 4.16 for all b ∈ (−1/2, 1/2).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/1367-kelly-criterion-simple-random-walk-levy-processes.md", "equation": "Admissibility conditions: P(r ≥ −1) = 1 (losses bounded by 100%, eq. 2.2); P(r>0)>0 and P(r<0)>0 (eq. 2.3); E", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9133}
